    <string name="panel_season_river">Water at %1$s varies much more across a year than across a day. Runoff, rainfall and wind can lift or lower the entire daily tide.</string>
    <string name="panel_season_tide">The water at %1$s follows a daily tide and a yearly cycle of comparable size. The timing of a high or low stays predictable as the seasonal level changes.</string>
    <string name="panel_spring_explain">The Sun and Moon pull along the same line. Their combined effect tends to widen the tidal range.</string>
    <string name="panel_neap_explain">At quarter moon the Sun and Moon pull at right angles. The tidal range tends to narrow.</string>
    <string name="panel_perigee_explain">The Moon is near its closest point to Earth, where its tidal pull is stronger.</string>
    <string name="panel_apogee_explain">The Moon is near its farthest point from Earth, where its tidal pull is weaker.</string>
